  "body": {
    "type": "doc",
    "content": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "This recipe serves 2 and is ready in under 10 minutes. It is one of the simplest Japanese dishes you can make."
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": ""
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Ochazuke"
          },
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "is a way to use leftover rice. Hot tea transforms a bowl of plain rice into a light, savoury meal."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "Use freshly brewed, hot green tea. Brew it a little stronger than you would for drinking. Pour it slowly over the rice rather than stirring, so the rice stays in place and the toppings stay on top."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "attrs": {
          "level": 2
        },
        "content": [
          {
            "type": "text",
            "text": "What you need"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "ingredientsList",
        "attrs": {
          "defaultServings": 2,
          "items": [
            {
              "ingredientSlug": "japanese-short-grain-rice",
              "amount": 300,
              "unit": "g",
              "prepNote": "cooked, hot or reheated",
              "isOptional": false,
              "groupLabel": null
            },
            {
              "ingredientSlug": "green-tea",
              "amount": 400,
              "unit": "ml",
              "prepNote": "freshly brewed, hot",
              "isOptional": false,
              "groupLabel": null
            },
            {
              "ingredientSlug": "nori",
              "amount": 2,
              "unit": "sheets",
              "prepNote": "cut into thin strips",
              "isOptional": false,
